# Headers for the paths that wrangler.jsonc's run_worker_first now excludes
# from the Worker (the content-hashed bundles and the five vendored asset
# trees). Cloudflare does NOT apply this file to a response the Worker
# generates — so worker/security-headers.ts and worker/asset-cache.ts still
# own every other path, and this file owns exactly the paths those two no
# longer see. Keep the header values identical to those two files; they are
# the same policy, just reached by a different route for these nine patterns.
#
# Each pattern gets its own block rather than sharing one broader rule,
# because the immutable Cache-Control belongs only to the four content-hashed
# bundle patterns and must never reach the five vendored trees, which keep
# stable filenames across a deploy and would otherwise be stuck on a year-old
# copy — the same reasoning asset-cache.ts documents for /sw.js.

/main-*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()

